missile-defense (0.9.1-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Windows installer: the Start-menu shortcut pointed at
    bin\missile-defense.exe, one directory below where the game actually
    lands — an entry with no icon that opened nothing, and a finish page
    whose "run Missile Defense" box failed the same way. CPack's NSIS
    generator assumes executables live in bin/ unless told otherwise; it is
    now told.
  * Windows: starting the installed game flashed a console window for every
    Python interpreter probed before the game window appeared. The probe ran
    through _popen, which cannot ask for CREATE_NO_WINDOW; it now spawns the
    interpreter directly, windowless. Only an installed build probes (a
    checkout ships no wheel), which is why no developer ever saw it.
  * Windows: ENTER on "THE TRAINER IS NOT INSTALLED" visibly did nothing.
    The install terminal was spawned through QProcess, which opens console
    children of a GUI process with no window and escapes quotes in a way
    cmd.exe does not read — an invisible cmd holding a mangled command,
    once per keypress. It now gets its own console window and a verbatim
    command line.
  * The TRAIN AI notice for an out-of-date trainer said "PRESS ENTER TO
    UPDATE IT" but opened the instructions page instead. ENTER now runs the
    update it promised.
  * CI: the check that the trainer wheel was staged beside the game guarded
    on an environment variable no step ever set, so it had never run. It is
    unconditional now on both installer legs (Windows and macOS).
  * TRAIN AI now notices a finished install without restarting the game.
    The machine was probed once at startup, so the menu kept answering
    "not installed" after the terminal it had spawned itself said
    otherwise. Anything short of a ready trainer is re-probed each time
    TRAIN AI is chosen — which also notices updates and a Python installed
    mid-session.
  * Windows: the install terminal now opens in front of the game and at a
    fixed 100x30 size. It used to open behind the window that spawned it,
    at whatever size the user's console defaults said — bigger than the
    screen, on the machine that reported it.
  * OPTIONS: the AI SKILL row is gone. It chose the scripted rung WATCH AI
    ran, a decision the WATCH AI submenu has since taken over by naming
    all three rungs itself; the row set something nothing read.

 -- Jens Köhler <jens@koehler-speyer.de>  Wed, 29 Jul 2026 00:30:14 +0200

missile-defense (0.9.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Numbered 0.9.0 rather than 1.0.0 because the macOS build is untested:
    it compiles and its tests pass, but nobody has yet run it on a Mac.

